<DocsLayout
  title="Tolerance and tessellation"
  subtitle="How one chord-height tolerance decides segment counts, display decimals and curve tessellation across the CAD kernels."
  description="CADCAMFUN drawing tolerance: presets, segmentsFor and chordError, decimals, entity tessellation rules, and where each kernel takes its tolerance, with real outputs."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="purpose" class="doc-section">
    <h2>One tolerance, every curve</h2>
    <p>A tolerance is the largest distance the model may be from the true shape, in millimetres. For a circle drawn as a polygon that distance is the chord&apos;s sagitta r(1 − cos(π/n)), so the number of segments follows from the tolerance. <code>packages/core/src/cad/tolerance.ts</code> (39 lines) holds that rule; the editor&apos;s renderer, the assistant&apos;s element catalogue, the entity tessellator and the tests all use it.</p>
    <DocViewer3D title="Ø20 circle at three tolerances" caption="The same radius-10 circle as segmentsFor gives it: 10 segments at 0.5 mm (chord error 0.489), 23 at 0.1 mm (0.093) and 71 at the 0.01 mm default (0.0098). Each polygon is extruded 2 mm." solids={[{"kind":"extrude","profile":[[10.0,0.0],[8.09,5.878],[3.09,9.511],[-3.09,9.511],[-8.09,5.878],[-10.0,0.0],[-8.09,-5.878],[-3.09,-9.511],[3.09,-9.511],[8.09,-5.878]],"height":2,"color":"#c88a8a"},{"kind":"extrude","profile":[[35.0,0.0],[34.629,2.698],[33.544,5.196],[31.826,7.308],[29.601,8.879],[27.035,9.791],[24.318,9.977],[21.651,9.423],[19.233,8.17],[17.243,6.311],[15.828,3.984],[15.093,1.362],[15.093,-1.362],[15.828,-3.984],[17.243,-6.311],[19.233,-8.17],[21.651,-9.423],[24.318,-9.977],[27.035,-9.791],[29.601,-8.879],[31.826,-7.308],[33.544,-5.196],[34.629,-2.698]],"height":2,"color":"#c8a48a"},{"kind":"extrude","profile":[[60.0,0.0],[59.961,0.884],[59.844,1.761],[59.65,2.624],[59.38,3.466],[59.037,4.282],[58.623,5.064],[58.142,5.806],[57.597,6.503],[56.992,7.149],[56.333,7.739],[55.624,8.268],[54.872,8.733],[54.081,9.129],[53.258,9.454],[52.41,9.705],[51.542,9.88],[50.663,9.978],[49.779,9.998],[48.896,9.939],[48.022,9.802],[47.163,9.589],[46.327,9.301],[45.519,8.94],[44.747,8.509],[44.015,8.011],[43.331,7.451],[42.698,6.833],[42.123,6.16],[41.609,5.44],[41.161,4.677],[40.783,3.878],[40.476,3.048],[40.244,2.194],[40.088,1.324],[40.01,0.442],[40.01,-0.442],[40.088,-1.324],[40.244,-2.194],[40.476,-3.048],[40.783,-3.878],[41.161,-4.677],[41.609,-5.44],[42.123,-6.16],[42.698,-6.833],[43.331,-7.451],[44.015,-8.011],[44.747,-8.509],[45.519,-8.94],[46.327,-9.301],[47.163,-9.589],[48.022,-9.802],[48.896,-9.939],[49.779,-9.998],[50.663,-9.978],[51.542,-9.88],[52.41,-9.705],[53.258,-9.454],[54.081,-9.129],[54.872,-8.733],[55.624,-8.268],[56.333,-7.739],[56.992,-7.149],[57.597,-6.503],[58.142,-5.806],[58.623,-5.064],[59.037,-4.282],[59.38,-3.466],[59.65,-2.624],[59.844,-1.761],[59.961,-0.884]],"height":2,"color":"#8aa