  </section>

  <section id="constants" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Constants</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>TOLERANCE_PRESETS</td><td>0.1, 0.05, 0.01, 0.005, 0.002, 0.001, 0.0005</td><td>what the UI offers, coarse to fine</td></tr>
        <tr><td>DEFAULT_TOLERANCE</td><td>0.01</td><td>editor and tessellation default</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MIN_TOLERANCE</td><td>0.0001</td><td>below this isTolerance is false</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MAX_TOLERANCE</td><td>10</td><td>above this isTolerance is false</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MIN_CURVE_SEGMENTS</td><td>8</td><td>fewest segments of a circle</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MAX_CURVE_SEGMENTS</td><td>2048</td><td>default cap of segmentsFor</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MAX_SEGMENTS (tessellate.ts)</td><td>65 536</td><td>hard cap per entity in the entity tessellator</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MIN_TOLERANCE (tessellate.ts)</td><td>1e-6</td><td>floor so a zero tolerance cannot produce unbounded counts</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="tolerance.ts">
{"export const isTolerance: (value: unknown) => value is number      // finite, in [0.0001, 10]\n/** Smallest n \u2265 8 with r(1 \u2212 cos(\u03c0/n)) \u2264 tolerance, capped. */\nexport const segmentsFor: (radius: number, tolerance: number, cap?: number /* 2048 */) => number\nexport const chordError: (radius: number, segments: number) => number   // r(1 \u2212 cos(\u03c0/n))\n/** 0.001 \u2192 3, 0.05 \u2192 2, 0.5 \u2192 1; at most 6. */\nexport const decimalsForTolerance: (tolerance: number) => number"}
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="table" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Presets in numbers</h2>
    <p>Real <code>segmentsFor</code>, <code>chordError</code> and <code>decimalsForTolerance</code> output for each preset:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tolerance, mm</th><th>segments r 10</th><th>chord error r 10</th><th>decimals</th><th>segments r 50</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>0.1</td><td>23</td><td>9.314e-2</td><td>1</td><td>50</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0.05</td><td>32</td><td>4.815e-2</td><td>2</td><td>71</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0.01 (default)</td><td>71</td><td>9.788e-3</td><td>2</td><td>158</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0.005</td><td>100</td><td>4.934e-3</td><td>3</td><td>223</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0.002</td><td>158</td><td>1.977e-3</td><td>3</td><td>352</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0.001</td><td>223</td><td>9.923e-4</td><td>3</td><td>497</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0.0005</td><td>315</td><td>4.973e-4</td><td>4</td><td>703</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Edge cases, also real: <code>segmentsFor(1000, 0.0001)</code> = 2048 (the cap), <code>segmentsFor(2, 5)</code> = 8 (tolerance ≥ radius), <code>isTolerance(0.00005)</code> = false, <code>isTolerance(10)</code> = true, <code>decimalsForTolerance(0.0001)</code> = 4.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="entities" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Tessellating drawing entities</h2>
    <code>tessellate(entity, tolerance)</code> in <code>tessellate.ts</code> turns any drawing entity into polylines within the chord tolerance. That polyline is what the CAM layer offsets and what the viewport renders. A closed shape returns a ring whose first and last points differ; the closing segment is implicit.
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Entity</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Line</td><td>its two end points</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Circle, Arc</td><td>arc segment count from radius, sweep and tolerance, capped at 65 536</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ellipse</td><td>uniform parameter step h = √(8·tol / a), a the larger radius, at least 8 segments</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Spline</td><td>analytic bound of splinePolyline</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Polyline</td><td>bulged segments as arcs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rectangle</td><td>four corners</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Text, Dimension</td><td>no outline: empty list</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>For an ellipse with radii 20 and 10, <code>ellipseSegmentCount</code> gives 100 segments at 0.01 mm and 32 at 0.1 mm.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="where" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Where tolerances meet</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Kernel</th><th>Tolerance parameter</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Sketch profiles</td><td>sketchProfiles(sketch, tolerance)</td><td>0.01 mm</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mesh primitives</td><td>meshOf(solid, tolerance)</td><td>0.1 mm</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CSG coincidence</td><td>CsgOptions.tolerance</td><td>1e-7 × extent</td></tr>
        <tr><td>B-rep tessellation</td><td>TessellateOptions.chordTol</td><td>diagonal / 2000, in [0.001, 0.05]</td></tr>
        <tr><td>B-rep Boolean coincidence</td><td>BooleanOptions.tol</td><td>1e-8 × size, ≥ 1e-7</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Helix chords</td><td>stepsPerTurn</td><td>0.01 mm</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Display tolerance is not machining tolerance">
      <p>The drawing tolerance controls how curves are approximated. CAM verification and G-code arc fitting carry their own tolerances; see the CAM kernel.</p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>circles look polygonal</td><td>tolerance 0.1 on a large radius</td><td>choose a finer preset; segments grow with √r</td></tr>
        <tr><td>viewport slow on a large drawing</td><td>very fine tolerance on many curves</td><td>0.01 is enough for display; keep finer values for export</td></tr>
        <tr><td>length shows too many decimals</td><td>decimals follow the tolerance</td><td>decimalsForTolerance(0.01) = 2</td></tr>
        <tr><td>a value is rejected as tolerance</td><td>outside [0.0001, 10]</td><td>use a preset</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <DocRelated items={[{"title": "Kernel overview", "href": "/docs/kernels"}, {"title": "Mesh and CSG", "href": "/docs/kernels/mesh"}, {"title": "Exact B-rep", "href": "/docs/kernels/brep"}, {"title": "Viewport", "href": "/docs/viewport"}]} />
</DocsLayout>
